# MD (Annex B): remote identification for the application stage only. After screening clears, the
# applicant visits a branch; staff confirm the in-person ID check and the wet signature, and only then is the
# account opened and the card ordered. The difference is one config value: Activation: InBranch.

@onboarding = http://localhost:5100
@simulators = http://localhost:5300
@image = /9j/4EFUTEFTIFRFU1QgSU1BR0X/2Q==

### 1. Create in MD: 201 AWAITING_BRANCH_VISIT, nextAction VISIT_BRANCH. No core-banking call yet.
# @name create
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MD/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Tester",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "nationality": "XD",
  "countryOfResidence": "XD",
  "identifier": { "type": "NATIONAL_ID", "value": "1234567890", "issuingCountry": "XD" },
  "email": "applicant@example.test",
  "phone": "+15550100100",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "ID_CARD", "image": "{{image}}" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{image}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 2. A branch-staff token for MD.
# @name staff
POST {{simulators}}/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "branch", "market": "MD", "subject": "branch-md-1" }

### 3. What staff check against the physical ID: the details, identifier in full. Logged.
GET {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MD/branch/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staff.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Both confirmations are required (one missing gets 400). Then: 200 APPROVED.
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MD/branch/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}/activation
Authorization: Bearer {{staff.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identityDocumentChecked": true, "wetSignatureCollected": true }

### 5. The customer's view.
GET {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MD/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}
